1
00:00:03,109 --> 00:00:05,382
The volcano rumbles and spits lava!

2
00:00:05,432 --> 00:00:07,838
Mila steps back, Noah's eyes go wide.

3
00:00:07,888 --> 00:00:09,812
What is pushing all that out?

4
00:00:10,635 --> 00:00:12,785
Mila shakes a bottle of soda and…

5
00:00:12,835 --> 00:00:14,519
pop, it sprays everywhere!

6
00:00:14,569 --> 00:00:15,519
Noah is soaked…

7
00:00:15,569 --> 00:00:16,836
and he has an idea.

8
00:00:17,622 --> 00:00:19,136
Discovery mission!

9
00:00:21,665 --> 00:00:22,285
Mini mode!

10
00:00:22,335 --> 00:00:25,364
Under the volcano, the burning-hot rock melts…

11
00:00:25,414 --> 00:00:26,235
that's magma.

12
00:00:26,285 --> 00:00:28,779
And this magma, lighter than the rock,

13
00:00:28,829 --> 00:00:30,771
rises like a bubble in syrup.

14
00:00:31,560 --> 00:00:34,727
Inside this magma, gas is squeezed by the pressure.

15
00:00:34,777 --> 00:00:36,998
But as it rises, the pressure drops…

16
00:00:37,048 --> 00:00:38,575
and the gas makes bubbles

17
00:00:38,625 --> 00:00:40,139
that push the magma out!

18
00:00:40,924 --> 00:00:42,491
If the magma rises slowly,

19
00:00:42,541 --> 00:00:45,165
the gas escapes gently, and the lava flows.

20
00:00:45,215 --> 00:00:46,471
But if it rises fast,

21
00:00:46,521 --> 00:00:48,399
the gas bursts out all at once…

22
00:00:48,449 --> 00:00:50,128
boom, the volcano explodes!

23
00:00:50,901 --> 00:00:52,981
Outside, magma is called lava.

24
00:00:53,031 --> 00:00:55,111
Red and burning hot, it flows,

25
00:00:55,161 --> 00:00:57,028
then cools into black rock…

26
00:00:57,078 --> 00:00:59,918
and the volcano grows, little by little.

27
00:01:00,720 --> 00:01:03,225
And that's why volcanoes erupt.

28
00:01:04,265 --> 00:01:06,374
Magma rises because it is lighter,

29
00:01:06,424 --> 00:01:08,455
and its gas bubbles push it out.

30
00:01:09,720 --> 00:01:11,171
Outside, with an adult:

31
00:01:11,221 --> 00:01:13,455
shake a bottle of soda and open it.

32
00:01:13,505 --> 00:01:15,413
The bubbles push the soda out,

33
00:01:15,463 --> 00:01:17,486
just like gas pushes the magma!

34
00:01:18,262 --> 00:01:20,778
And how does sound travel to our ears?

35
00:01:20,828 --> 00:01:22,178
The answer tomorrow.
